[[0,1409862,0,1,0,1,"2016-11-14T00:49:08","DrudgeBot","",[],"","REX REED: Mel Gibson 'HACKSAW RIDGE' Best War Film In 20 Years...","http://observer.com/2016/11/mel-gibsons-hacksaw-ridge-is-the-best-war-film-since-saving-private-ryan/","Drudge"],[1,6815821,0,0,0,0,"2016-11-14T00:50:10","derram","",[],"<p><a href=\"https://archive.is/HlzDw\">https://archive.is/HlzDw</a> : \n</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>Mel Gibson’s ‘Hacksaw Ridge’ is the Best War Film Since ‘Saving Private Ryan’ | | Observer </p>\n</blockquote>\n<p>' The one who redefined the word hope on Hacksaw Ridge is a good place to start. ' </p>\n<p>'Like the voters who plan to stay home on Election Day because they don’t like the candidates, potential filmgoers who avoid Hacksaw Ridge because they object to Mel Gibson will be the losers. ' </p>\n<p>'The screaming noise and nerve-crushing tempos of battle fury come crashing down like nothing since Saving Private Ryan. ' </p>\n<p>'Burning bodies, severed limbs, stepping on intestines and sleeping in foxholes with rats crawling out of severed heads are common. ' </p>\n<p>'Mel Gibson recreates the life of an extraordinary patriot at a time when a troubled world, guided by a sadly compromised American leadership, could use a role model. ' </p>\n<p><a href=\"https://vgy.me/cuvskM.png\">This has been an automated message.</a></p>"],[1,6815864,0,0,0,0,"2016-11-14T00:56:30","Butelczynski","[e]",[],"<p>I haven't seen it yet but there was a lot of really good war movies over last 20 years.Enemy At The Gates comes to mind,few Chinese movies were great too.</p>"]]
